ner_results: ```plaintext
4. <1>Lytic S1 vertebral body lesion</1>: <2>maximum SUV of 6.6</2>. <3>Lymph nodes</3>: Index nodes as described above. Additional <4>hypermetabolic right internal mammary node</4> is <5>0.6 x 0.8 cm</5> (series 4 1 image 75 with a <6>maximum SUV of 4.3</6>. The <7>hypermetabolic caudate lobe lesion</7> is markedly increased in size when compared to prior <8>CT abdomen/pelvis</8> from <9>09/29/2018</9>. Additional <10>hypoattenuating, hypermetabolic segment VII lesion</10> is <11>1.3 x 1.7 x 1.5 cm</11> with a <12>maximum SUV of 11.2</12> <13>02/25/19 Liver biopsy</13>: <14>triple negative metastatic breast cancer</14> *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/***** <15>Abraxane</15> and <16>Pembrolizumab</16> <17>05/31/19 PET/CT</17>: significantly increased number and extent of <18>hypermetabolic metastases</18> including <19>osseous</19>, <20>hepatic</20>, <21>nodal</21>, and <22>chest wall lesions</22>. New <23>linear hypermetabolism</23> extending along the central and left aspect of <24>clivus</24> and <25>petrous bone</25> with suggestion of possible underlying <26>osseous irregularity</26>, concerning for <27>intracranial and/or skull base involvement</27> but incompletely evaluated on this exam. New <28>hypermetabolic lesions in bilateral femoral necks</28>, which may place patient at risk for <29>pathologic fracture</29>. *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/***** admitted to ***** with <30>fever</30>, <31>chest pain/swelling</31>, and <32>low back pain</32>. Found to have <33>chest wall cellulitis</33> and given <34>ABX</34>. Imaging done - see below. <35>06/11/19 MRI lumbar spine</35>: Numerous <36>bone marrow replacing lesion</36> in the <37>lumbar spine</37> and in the <38>pelvis</38>, most pronounced at <39>S1 with endplate fracture</39>. <40>06/13/19 CT CAP</40>: Interval development of <41>subcutaneous edema</41> in the <42>ventral chest wall soft tissues</42>, without drainable fluid collection, suspicious for <43>soft tissue infection/cellulitis</43>. Slightly more hypodense appearance of enhancing nodules in the <44>right chest wall</44> and <45>right pectoralis musculature</45>. Unchanged adjacent <46>right internal mammary lymphadenopathy</46>. New <47>trace pleural effusions</47> with increase in <48>pericardial recess</48>.
``` 
