<1>nodules</1> or <2>pleural-based</2>. There are areas of <3>subsegmental atelectasis</3> in both <4>lungs</4>. There are no <5>pleural effusions</5>. <6>Mediastinal and hilar lymphadenopathy</6> identified. <7>Mediastinal lymph nodes</7> measure up to 15 mm. Largest <8>hilar lymph nodes</8> are present with a <9>left hilar lymph node</9> measuring up to 15 mm. There are multiple enlarged <10>cardiophrenic angle lymph nodes</10>. There are enlarged <11>internal mammary lymph nodes</11> on the right. There is extensive <12>right axillary lymphadenopathy</12>. <13>Nodes</13> measure up to 21 x 18 mm. Multiple <14>nodules</14> are present in the upper inner <15>right breast</15>, one of which is inseparable from the underlying <16>pectoral muscles</16>. There is <17>skin thickening</17> over the central <18>breast</18> and there is an irregularly marginated <19>mass</19> within the <20>breast</20> centrally located above the <21>nipple</21> measuring over 6 cm. There are multiple small <22>lymph nodes</22> in the upper <23>abdomen</23>. <24>Portacaval lymph node</24> measures up to 30 x 15 mm. Small <25>para-aortic lymph nodes</25> are also present less than 1 cm. There is widespread <26>osseous metastatic disease</26>. <27>Pathologic destruction</27> of multiple <28>ribs</28> and extensive distraction of the <29>sternum</29> involving body of the <30>sternum</30> as well as the <31>manubrium</31>. There is involvement of the <32>thoracic spine</32> most severe at <33>T10</33> where there is involvement of the <34>vertebral body</34> the <35>pedicle</35> and there is intraspinal extension along the right and lateral aspects of the <36>canal</36>. There is involvement of the right <37>pedicle L1</37> as well.  02/10/18 <38>MRI Lumbar spine w/ and w/o contrast</38>: Abnormal <39>marrow signal</39> with replacement of normal <40>marrow</40> throughout the <41>lumbosacral spine</41> consistent with <42>metastatic infiltration</42>. <43>Sacral tissues</43> are also infiltrated. There is mild <44>fracture</44> of the inferior endplate of <45>L1</45> on the right side. <46>T12 inferior endplate</46> demonstrates <47>fracture</47> mild loss of height as well. <48>Epidural contrast enhancement</48> ventrally and dorsally consistent with <49>metastases</49>. This is ***** at <50>L5 level</50>. Abnormal replacement of the <51>marrow signal</51> with <52>tumor</52>.
``` 
