ner_results: ```plaintext
There is no edema in the adjacent brain parenchyma. <1>Ureteral based metastases</1> are present along the <2>posterior interhemispheric falx</2> and <3>parasagittal convexity</3> bilaterally. There is no edema in the adjacent brain parenchyma. Additionally, small punctate foci of <4>contrast enhancement</4> are noted in the <5>right cerebellar hemisphere</5> inferiorly and posteriorly. It is not clear whether these are small <6>parenchymal metastases</6> or <7>meningeal tumor</7>. There is an approximately <8>15 mm metastases</8> in the <9>upper clivus</9> (<10>skull</10>). <11>02/10/17: BRCA1/2 negative</11>. <12>02/11/17 CT A/P w/ contrast</12>: <13>Right breast skin thickening</13> is partially imaged. <14>Minimal bibasilar atelectasis</14>. <15>Right lower lobe posterior medial soft tissue thickening</15> along the <16>pleural surface</16>. Few small <17>right cardiophrenic angle lymph nodes</17> are more numerous than normally seen. <18>Small retroperitoneal lymph nodes</18> are predominantly under 1 cm. <19>Extensive bony lytic destructive appearance</19> to the <20>left inferior pubic ramus</20> with <21>subacute/healing fractures</21> suggested. <22>Old right inferior pubic ramus fracture</22> is also seen as well as <23>lytic appearance of the left greater than right acetabulum</23>. <24>Small nondisplaced fracture of the left sacral ala</24> likely pathologic with <25>diffuse osseous metastatic involvement</25> of the <26>sacrum</26> and <27>iliac bones</27> as well as throughout the <28>lumbar vertebral bodies</28> and in <29>multiple ribs</29>. <30>Several healing left and right rib fractures</30> are seen also likely pathologic. <31>Mild degenerative disc disease L4-5</31>. <32>Several endplate compression fracture deformities</32>, for example, <33>inferior endplate compression of T12</33>. <34>Large lytic lesion</34> destroys and replaces much of <35>T10</35>. <36>02/11/17 bilateral diagnostic mammogram</36> and <37>limited right breast US</37>: The <38>breast tissue</38> is fatty with <39>scattered fibroglandular elements</39>. In the <40>right breast</40> at <41>12 o'clock middle third</41>, there is a <42>large spiculated mass</42> containing <43>numerous suspicious calcifications</43>. There is <44>diffuse overlying skin thickening</44> as well. No suspicious findings.
``` 
