 are seen in the left breast on <1>mammography</1>. <2>High-resolution ultrasound</2> of the <3>right breast</3>: At 12 o'clock, 2 cm from the nipple, there is a <4>hypoechoic heterogeneous irregularly shaped mass</4> measuring at least 10 x 5 x 7 cm corresponding to <5>mammographic findings</5> and <6>palpable mass</6>. In the <7>right axilla</7>, there is a <8>25 mm lymph node</8> with <9>thickened cortex</9> that is suspicious for additional <10>metastases</10>.  02/14/17 <11>CT-guided biopsy</11> of the <12>posterior superior left iliac bone</12>: +<13>metastatic adenocarcinoma of breast origin</13>, <14>ER+(76%)</14>/<15>PR+(33%)</15>/*****+ (<16>IHC 3+</16>, no <17>FISH</17> done)  02/14/17 *****-guided biopsy of <18>R breast mass</18>: +<19>IDC</19>, <20>moderately differentiated</20>, <21>ER+(97%)</21>/<22>PR+(79%)</22>/*****+ (<23>IHC 3+</23>/<24>FISH 15.April 10=5.4</24>)  02/18/17: <25>EF 76%</25>  02/18/17 <26>CT A/P</26> due to <27>hypotension</27> and <28>lower extremity weakness</28>: stable compared to 02/11/17 but new <29>left gluteus medius intermuscular hematoma</29>.  02/18/17: new <30>anemia</30> of unclear etiology other than new <31>hematoma</31> (site of <32>bone biopsy</32>)  *****/*****/*****- *****/*****/***** <33>complete 10 fractions (30 Gy) to T spine</33>  02/23/17: start <34>herceptin</34> and ***** (no <35>chemo</35> given due to <36>anemia</36>), start <37>letrozole</37>  03/14/17: second dose <38>herceptin</38> and *****  03/18/17: discharged to ***** *****, *****, ***** for <39>rehab</39>  04/20/17: Consult Dr. ***** (UCSF), only on <40>letrozole</40> at this point, no h/p since *****  05/04/17: start <41>taxotere 75mg/m2</41> and resume <42>herceptin</42> and *****  *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/*****: admitted locally with <43>severe sepsis</43>, <44>neutropenic fever</44>, <45>n/v</45>  *****/*****: second dose <46>taxotere 75mg/m2</46>, <47>herceptin</47> and *****  *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/*****: admitted locally <48>anemia</48>, <49>mucositis</49>, <50>neutropenic fever</50>, <51>n/v</51>
