early stage *****+/*****- <1>IDC</1> of the <2>left breast</2> diagnosed in 2009 s/p <3>bilateral mastectomies</3> and 5 years of <4>Tamoxifen</4>, now with metastatic recurrence with disease in the <5>bone</5> and <6>lymph nodes</6>. We had an extensive discussion regarding her diagnosis and potential treatment options. Given her cancer is <7>HR+</7> and *****- we discussed that her treatment will include <8>hormonal therapy</8>. We discussed use of <9>CDK February 26 inhibitors</9> in combination with ***** for first line treatment. We reviewed the data from the ***** ***** which demonstrated ***** postmenopausal women with <10>ER-positive</10>, *****-negative <11>breast cancer</11> who were randomized to receive <12>letrozole</12> plus <13>palbociclib</13> had a median <14>PFS</14> of 24.8 months (compared with 14.5 months in the placebo). The most common adverse events were <15>neutropenia</15>, <16>anemia</16>, and <17>fatigue</17>. We also reviewed the anticipated side effects and risks associated with <18>aromatase inhibitors</18> including but not limited to <19>arthralgias</19>, <20>urogenital atrophy</20>, and possible acceleration of <21>bone density loss/fractures</21>, and discussed strategies to mitigate these side effects. She has consented to treatment and thus <22>letrozole</22> has been sent to ***** *****. <23>Palbociclib</23> has been sent to the ***** ***** *****. We discussed potential <24>palbociclib</24> side effects including but not limited to <25>myelosuppression</25> in particular <26>neutropenia</26> requiring count checks every 4 weeks before the start of the next cycle, as well as <27>mucositis</27>, <28>fatigue</28>, <29>n/v</29>, <30>hair thinning</30>, <31>pneumonitis</31>. Since she has extensive <32>bony mets</32> and new <33>pain</33>, we recommend obtaining new scans and ordered <34>MRI of total spine</34> and <35>CAP CT</35>. We will request her outside <36>PET/CT</36> for comparison. We also discussed that in patients with <37>breast cancer</37> with <38>bone metastases</38>, use of <39>bone modifying agents</39> reduce the risk of <40>skeletal related events</40>. Thus, we recommend initiation of <41>denosumab</41>. We recommend that she have <42>dental clearance</42> prior to its initiation and reviewed potential <43>AEs</43>.
