ner_results: ```plaintext
suspicious mass in the <1>left breast</1>.  <2>10/30/2008</2> the patient underwent a <3>fine-needle aspiration</3> that revealed an <4>invasive ductal carcinoma</4> which was <5>estrogen receptor positive</5>, <6>progesterone receptor negative</6>, and <7>HER-2/neu negative</7>.  <8>12/18/2008</8> the patient underwent a <9>left breast lumpectomy</9> and <10>sentinel lymph node biopsy</10>.  Pathology revealed a <11>1.5 cm grade 3 invasive ductal carcinoma</11> which was <12>estrogen receptor positive</12>, <13>progesterone receptor negative</13>, and <14>HER-2 negative</14> by <15>immunohistochemistry</15>.  One out of the <16>3 sentinel lymph nodes</16> was positive.  In <17>December 2008</17> the patient had a <18>completion axillary lymph node dissection</18> and only <19>2 lymph nodes</19> were seen both negative for cancer.  In <20>January 2009</20>, the patient initiated <21>chemotherapy</21> with <22>Cytoxan</22>, <23>methotrexate</23>, and <24>5-*****</24>.  She also started <25>Lupron</25> at this time.  The patient underwent <26>genetic testing</26> and was negative for <27>BRCA1</27> and <28>2</28>.  <29>08/27/2009</29> the patient underwent a <30>CT scan of the chest abdomen and pelvis</30> revealing enhancing tissue in the <31>right anterior breast</31>, a <32>sclerotic focus in the left sacral ala</32>, and a <33>new sclerotic focus in the right anterior superior acetabulum</33>. A <34>bone scan</34> on <35>09/04/2009</35> revealed no uptake to suggest <36>osseous metastasis</36>.  <37>09/12/2009</37> the patient initiated <38>postoperative radiation</38> to the <39>left breast</39>, <40>supraclavicular</40>, and <41>axillary regions</41> receiving <42>1800 cGY</42> to these regions.  <43>09/20/2009</43>, the patient underwent a <44>core biopsy</44> of a mass in the <45>12:00 position of the right breast</45> which revealed a <46>grade 1 invasive ductal carcinoma</46>.  <47>11/08/2009</47>, the patient underwent a <48>PET CT scan</48> at ***** revealing <49>skin thickening in the right breast</49>, a <50>1.1 cm area of soft tissue enhancement in the right breast</50>, no <51>axillary or internal mammary adenopathy</51>, and no clear evidence of <52>distant metastatic disease</52>.  <53>12/14/2009</53> the patient underwent <54>bilateral mastectomies</54>, <55>bilateral ***** flap reconstruction</55>, and a <56>left completion axillary</56>
``` 
