 in situ, intermediate nuclear grade with <1>comedo necrosis</1>; see comment.  3.  ***** changes and <2>apocrine metaplasia</2>.  4.  Biopsy site changes.  5.  <3>Microcalcifications</3> associated with <4>invasive carcinoma</4>.       C.  <5>Right breast</5>, "anterior, inferior, medial, posterior margin of right  <6>partial mastectomy</6>," <7>re-excision</7>:   1.  <8>Ductal carcinoma in situ</8>, intermediate nuclear grade, focally  present at the true margin; see comment.  2.  <9>Apocrine metaplasia</9>.  3.  <10>Microcalcifications</10> associated with <11>benign ducts</11>.       D.  <12>Right breast</12>, nodule from areolar at 12:30, <13>excisional biopsy</13>:  1.  <14>Invasive carcinoma</14> with mixed <15>micropapillary</15> and <16>ductal features</16>, modified ***** <17>grade 2</17>, 0.6 cm, present at the true margin; see comment.  2.  <18>Ductal carcinoma in situ</18>, intermediate nuclear grade, margins  negative.  3.  <19>Microcalcifications</19> associated with <20>invasive carcinoma</20>.      E.  <21>Right breast skin</21>, <22>excision</22>:  <23>Benign skin</23>.   COMMENT:  <24>Breast Tumor Synoptic Comment</24>   - Laterality:  <25>Right</25>.  - Procedure:  *****-localized <26>partial mastectomy</26> (part B) and  <27>excisional biopsy</27> (part D).  - Tumor site:  ***** tumor at 11:30, 7 cm from the nipple (part B);  smaller tumor at 12:30 (part D).  - Invasive tumor type:  <28>Invasive carcinoma</28> with mixed <29>micropapillary</29> and  <30>ductal features</30>. For larger tumor in part B: the micropapillary  component comprises ~80% of the tumor. For the smaller tumor in part  D, the micropapillary component is ~60%.  - Invasive tumor size:  Two foci. The larger tumor: 1.6 cm (part B).  Tumor size determined based on tumor present in 3 consecutive slices  (slices 7 to 9, ***** thickness 0.55 cm). The smaller tumor: 0.6 cm  (part D). Tumor size based on largest dimension on slide D1.  - Invasive tumor grade (modified *****-*****-*****):  Both tumors  show similar morphology with same ***** grade. The following is based on  the larger tumor:- Nuclear grade:  2 points.       - Mitotic count:  October 21 *****, 1 
``` 
