<1>adjuvant chemotherapy</1> and <2>hormonal therapy</2>. She understands that she will need to undergo <3>re-excision</3> for the margin positive for <4>non-invasive cancer</4> and she also understands the role of <5>post-lumpectomy radiation</5>. She has met with Dr. ***** in ***** *****. *****. ***** reviewed the meaning of the ***** result and described the data for use of ***** as both a prognostic and predictive tool. We explained the published results from the ***** trial which demonstrated that patients who have clinical higher risk cancers based on traditional measures including <6>tumor size</6>, <7>grade</7> and <8>lymph node status</8>, but whose tumors have a ***** Low Risk profile have an excellent prognosis at 5 years even in the absence of chemotherapy, and chemotherapy offers very little benefit for these patients. Given this is *****'s situation, Dr. ***** does not recommend chemotherapy. In terms of hormonal therapy, we explained that <9>aromatase inhibitors</9> have been shown to have improved outcomes in terms of <10>DFS</10> as compared to <11>tamoxifen</11>. The decision regarding continuing hormone therapy for 5 versus 10 years will be considered later and will largely depend on *****'s tolerance of hormonal therapy. We reviewed the anticipated side effects and risks associated with an aromatase inhibitors including <12>arthralgias</12>, <13>urogenital atrophy</13>, and possible acceleration of <14>bone density loss</14>. We explained that the <15>joint pains</15> are often the most difficult side effect to manage, and not infrequently, patients will switch to another aromatase inhibitor, and if not able to tolerate, we will consider switching to tamoxifen. In regards to efficacy, there are three <16>AIs</16> and all are equivalent, although some patients tolerate one better than another. Therefore, we will recommend she start <17>letrozole 2.5mg PO daily</17>. We discussed that while on hormone therapy, she should undergo assessment for <18>bone health</18>, specifically a <19>bone density scan</19>.
``` 
