   ***** has had an unfortunate local <1>relapse</1>. This is actually her second local <2>relapse</2> following a rapid early local <3>relapse</3> in <4>2012</4>. She did enjoy an <5>8 year disease-free interval</5> but the current local <6>relapse</6> ***** a high risk of future <7>relapse</7> and <8>mortality</8> from this <9>disease</9>.    The benefit of <10>chemotherapy</10> in reducing her <11>recurrence risk</11> and <12>mortality</12> was reviewed. This was the subject of the <13>CALOR study</13> which showed that <14>adjuvant chemotherapy</14> following <15>resection</15> of local <16>recurrences</16> benefits ***** with <17>ER negative disease</17>, but does not benefit patients with <18>ER positive disease</18> (***** ***** *****). I don't think ***** will benefit from <19>chemotherapy</19> at this point.    ***** will benefit from the resumption of <20>hormonal therapy</20>. Her <21>recurrence</21> did occur a year after stopping <22>anastrozole</22> against medical advice, so potentially this <23>disease</23> remains ***** sensitive. On the other hand, the <24>disease</24> is naive to <25>tamoxifen</25> and this may be a more effective option in this case, specially considering the possibility of *****-resistant clonal ***** mutations that may have arisen during the years of ***** <26>therapy</26>. Side effects of <27>tamoxifen</27> were discussed including the potential for <28>thromboembolic phenomenon</28> including <29>DVT</29> and <30>PE</30> and <31>endometrial cancers</31>.     ***** has had two local <32>recurrences</32> and will benefit from <33>chest wall RT</33>. She declined this previously which is unfortunate, but she accepts a referral now. ***** refer to ***** for consultation.    In summary the plan is:  - check <34>labs</34>  - <35>tamoxifen 20mg PO qD</35>  - referral to *****  - return to clinic in <36>6 months</36>      
``` 
