 of 2011 she had no gastrointestinal complaints whatsoever.  She had no <1>abdominal pain</1>, no change in <2>bowel habit</2>, no <3>nausea</3> or <4>vomiting</4>.  The patient was given a course of <5>prednisone</5> and <6>antibiotics</6> for a <7>sinus infection</7>, and following this for her <8>abdominal complaints</8> started.  She says that on balance her complaints are a bit better.  She still has <9>abdominal gas</9> and <10>bloating</10>, and some irregularity of <11>bowel habit</11> and recurrent <12>nausea</12>.  However she denies any recent episodes of severe cramping <13>abdominal pain</13> at least for the last one to 2 months.  Despite the symptoms the patient has not lost any significant amount of weight.  She has not had any <14>vomiting of blood</14> or <15>rectal bleeding</15>.  She denies any <16>fevers</16> or <17>chills</17>.  The patient had a <18>colonoscopy</18> in 2010 soon before the onset of the symptoms and that was normal by her report.  She was seen by her primary physician and Dr. ***** for these complaints, and no significant abnormalities were found during their evaluation.  By her report she had routine laboratory studies including a <19>celiac antibody profile</19> was normal.  She also underwent an <20>upper endoscopy</20> with <21>biopsy</21> throughout the <22>upper GI tract</22> and was only notable for a slight increase in intraepithelial lymphocytes found on the <23>duodenal biopsy</23> but otherwise was a normal exam.  The patient has been treated with <24>dexilant</24> for the past few months, she is uncertain if this medication has made much of a difference.         Stage at *****:  <25>Cancer Staging</25>  <26>Infiltrating ductal carcinoma of upper-outer quadrant of left breast</26> in female (CMS code)  Staging form: <27>Breast, AJCC 8th Edition</27>  - Pathologic: <28>Stage IIA</28> (<29>pT2</29>, *****(*****+)(sn), *****, *****, <30>ER-</30>, <31>PR-</31>, *****-) - Signed by ***** ***** *****, MD on 08/25/2020     