 continues to recover from <1>surgery</1>. She met with Dr. ***** in <2>radiation oncology</2> today and elected to enrolled on a <3>clinic trial</3>, which will randomized her to 3 vs 5 weeks of <4>radiation</4>. Tentative start date is 12/16/18. We discussed the role of <5>endocrine therapy</5> today. She start an <6>aromatase inhibitor</6> after she completes radiation. She has decided to proceed with a <7>bilateral oophorectomy</7> with Dr. *****, so she may not require <8>ovarian suppression</8>. Dr. ***** also discussed she may be eligible for the ***** trial with <9>ribociclib</9> that should open around the time she completes radiation.    2. <10>Pulmonary nodule</10>: Baseline <11>PET/CT</11> in April 2018 showed a non-specific <12>4 mm pulmonary nodule</12>. Her <13>CT Chest</13> in August 2018 was stable. Consider a follow up <14>CT Chest</14> in one year.     3. <15>Low weight</15>, improved: We encouraged her to continue efforts to gain weight. Continue small, frequent meals a day and <16>Ensure protein shakes</16>. Continue to trend weight. Follow up with <17>nutrition</17> on 11/30/18.    4. <18>Anxiety</18>: She continues to struggle with anxiety though she states this is slightly improved. Encouraged her to follow up with her local therapist. She was prescribed <19>Lexapro</19> previously but has not taken it.    5. <20>BRCA1 mutation</20>: S/p <21>bilateral mastectomy</21>. She will see Dr. ***** on 12/02/18 to discuss bilateral oophorectomy.     6. <22>Pain in neck and back</22> and <23>limited ROM in bilateral arms</23>: Referred to <24>PT</24>.     Follow up on 01/05/19       This is a shared visit for services provided by me, ***** ***** *****, MD. I performed a face-to-face encounter with the patient and the following portion of the note is my own.     I have reviewed the history and participated in the physical exam and assessment and plan as documented.    Additional A/P: ***** looks a little stronger today and has gained a few pounds. Per the NP note, ***** will undergo a <25>BSO</25> eventually, but depending on timing, she may not need <26>OS</26> if she does not recover <27>ovarian</27> 
