WRN 01/14/21 ***** <1>abdomen</1>: 1. No MRI correlate to the previously described <2>1.5 cm hypodensity</2> within the <3>left hepatic lobe</3>. The previously described <4>vascular irregularity</4> of the <5>left inferior renal artery</5> is seen, but better characterized on prior <6>CTA exam</6>. 01/20/21 start <7>neoadjuvant taxol</7> ***** followed by ***** 06/02/21 ***** *****: RIGHT <8>Breast</8>: Interval decrease in volume, extent and avidity of enhancement of the known <9>right upper inner malignancy</9> with residual segmental <10>non-mass enhancement</10> measuring up to <11>28 x 10 x 25 mm</11> (AP x trans x CC extent) on <12>MIP images</12> (previously measuring up to <13>38 x 14 x 29 mm</13>). <14>Kinetic evaluation</14> demonstrates slow initial rise with delayed persistent enhancement. <15>Biopsy clip artifact</15> is noted along the anterolateral margin of the non-mass enhancement (axial <16>T1 non-FS image 46</16>). LEFT <17>Breast</17>: No abnormal areas of enhancement or other MRI features of <18>malignancy</18> are identified. OTHER: Decrease in size of <19>right level I and II axillary adenopathy</19> with <20>biopsy clip artifact</20> within a <21>biopsy proven nodal metastasis</21> (axial <22>T2 image 138</22>). No <23>left axillary adenopathy</23>. <24>Left chest port</24> ***** artifact.
``` 
