ner_results: ```plaintext
 corresponding formal radiology reports, as outlined in my Assessment/Plan     PATHOLOGY:   A. <1>Right breast axillary sentinel lymph nodes</1>:   - <2>2 lymph nodes involved by metastatic carcinoma</2> (each measuring up to 6   mm) (May 27)   - ***** <3>extranodal extension</3>   B. <4>Right breast, lumpectomy</4>   - <5>Invasive ductal carcinoma</5> (see comment and synoptic table)   C. <6>New right breast lateral-anterior margin</6>:   - Involved by <7>invasive ductal carcinoma</7> (see comment)   D. <8>Left breast tissue, excision</8>:   - <9>Benign breast tissue</9>   E. <10>Right breast skin, excision</10>:   - <11>Benign skin</11>   Comment: The <12>tumor</12> is fairly uniformly involving the <13>tumor bed</13> (measures   1.8 x 2.0 x 1.1 cm) and is present as single cells, small glands, and   small clusters with a cellularity of approximately 10-20%. <14>Tumor</14> is also   seen in the adjacent fat where it infiltrates in a fairly insidious   manner with the absence of significant stromal response. <15>Tumor cells</15> are   seen at multiple foci at the lateral margin and also focally at the   anterior margin. There is also a fair amount of <16>tumor cells</16> in the   additionally submitted <17>new right breast lateral-anterior margin</17> which   are also seen at the final margin in at least 2 foci (multifocal   involvement).     <18>CAP Synoptic Report</18>:<19>INVASIVE CARCINOMA OF THE BREAST</19>: <20>Resection</20>   (*****.0.1.3)   <21>Specimen Procedure</21>: <22>Excision</22> (less than total mastectomy)   <23>Specimen Laterality</23>: <24>Right</24>   <25>Tumor Histologic Type</25>: <26>Invasive carcinoma of no special type (ductal)</26>   <27>Histologic Grade</27> (***** Histologic Score):   <28>Glandular (Acinar) / Tubular Differentiation</28>: <29>Score 2</29>   <30>Nuclear Pleomorphism</30>: <31>Score 2</31>   <32>Mitotic Rate</32>: <33>Score 1</33>   <34>Overall Grade</34>: <35>Grade 1</35> (scores of 3, 4 or 5)   <36>Tumor Size</36>: <37>35 Millimeters (mm)</37> (***** 5)   <38>Ductal Carcinoma In Situ (DCIS)</38>: <39>Present</39>   <40>Architectural Patterns</40>: <41>Cribriform</41>   <42>Nuclear Grade</42>: <43>Grade II (intermediate)</43>   <44>Treatment Effect in the Breast</44>: <45>Probable or definite response</45> to 
``` 
