re-excision of <1>margins</1>. ***** send email to Dr. ***** and Dr. ***** regarding if an <2>axillary dissection</2> is recommended since she's going back to <3>surgery</3>.   -Pt's <4>port</4> was removed on <5>July 08</5> and she's worried that ***** ***** site is not healing as fast she she hoped. Reassured her there's no <6>s/sx of infection</6> and not concerned. Advised her to continue to monitor  -We will have her start <7>letrozole</7> now. <8>Rx</8> sent. We reviewed the potential side effects of ***** <9>therapy</9> which include but are not limited to <10>joint aches</10>, <11>hot flashes</11>, <12>dryness</12>, <13>hair thinning</13>, <14>weight gain</14>, <15>bone loss</15> and <16>increased risk of fracture</16>.  -Discussed addition of <17>abemaciclib</17> after completion of <18>xrt</18>.   -Baseline <19>dexa</19> ordered. .    -Encouraged her to fup with Dr. ***** in <20>rad onc</20> after her re-excision date is set.      <21>Granulomatous disease</21>  <22>Bronchoscopy</22> and <23>FNA of mediastinal nodes</23> on <24>01/09/21</24> was benign but showed granulomatous disease c/w <25>sarcoidosis</25>.  -Saw Dr. ***** in <26>sarcoid clinic</26> on <27>03/27/21</27>. Recommends <28>PFT</28>, <29>chest imaging</29> and <30>sarcoid related blood tests</30>.  -Saw <31>rheumatology</31> on <32>06/22/21</32> who did not feel she had any <33>systemic autoimmune disease</33>  -Fup with Dr. ***** and Dr. *****     <34>Joint pain</34>, <35>chronic</35>, improve  -unclear etiology, ?sarcoidosis. Saw rheumatology who did not feel she has any systemic autoimmune disease.   -Continue <36>naproxen 500mg bid</36>, <37>APAP</37> ok if taken sparingly  -Discussed <38>tramadol</38> if pain worsens/uncontrolled  -Discussed <39>PT</39> in the past       <40>Aneurysm of the distal renal artery</40>  -Seen on <41>CT abd angiogram</41> in <42>December 2020</42>  Saw Dr. ***** ***** <43>vascular surgery</43> on <44>01/26/21</44>. Does not rec <45>surgical intervention</45>. Her <46>renal artery u/s</46> was normal although she had <47>coffee AM</47> - unclear if that effects these results. If visualized, then <48>surveillance u/s imaging</48> in 1 year. Since not visualized, will obtain <49>MRA of the abdomen</49> in 1 year as well, due in <50>January 2022</50>  -Fup with Dr. *****     <51>Myalgias</51> likely due to <52>chemo</52>, unchanged   -Continue <53>naproxen 500mg BID</53>
