12:00 position, 7 cm from the nipple with extension posteriorly to the pectoralis muscle without muscle involvement. In addition, in the upper inner <1>left breast</1>, middle third, there was a <2>bilobed enhancing nodule</2> (1 cm), located 5 cm from the nipple, and 3 cm from the chest wall. A <3>lymph node</3> (2.5 cm) was present in the <4>left axilla</4> with associated <5>clip</5> as well as additional prominent asymmetric <6>left axillary LN</6>. The <7>right breast</7> was notable for <8>scattered cysts</8>, but no suspicious enhancing masses. She then underwent a <9>left breast US</9> to look at the <10>MRI-findings</10> at the 12:00 position demonstrated an area of <11>hypoechogenicity</11> (2.3 cm). A <12>left breast US-guided core biopsy</12> at the 12:00 position was notable for <13>invasive ductal carcinoma</13> with <14>ER+</14> (100%), <15>PR+</15> (100%), *****- (<16>IHC 2+</16>; <17>FISH ratio 1.4</17>). A <18>left breast US</18> to look at the <19>MRI-findings</19> at the 10:00 position demonstrated a <20>vague hypoechoic area</20>. A <21>left breast US-guided core biopsy</21> at the 10:00 position was notable for <22>invasive ductal carcinoma</22>, also with <23>ER+</23> (100%), <24>PR+</24> (100%), *****- (<25>IHC 0</25>). This <26>biopsy</26> was sent for ***** and resulted as <27>low risk</27> with a <28>score of 11</28>. She underwent a <29>PET with CT</29> for attenuation purposes on 11/22/16 demonstrated no uptake in known <30>left axillary LN metastasis</30> or in the <31>left breast</31>, however, uptake in the <32>bone marrow</32> of <33>T7-L1</33> was slightly more prominent, of unclear significance. A <34>thoracic spine MRI</34> on 12/07/16 was notable for no evidence of <35>metastases</35>. She has met with Dr. ***** ***** in ***** ***** who recommended <36>neoadjuvant dose-dense AC</36> followed by <37>paclitaxel</37> as well as Dr. ***** at ***** ***** ***** who recommended proceeding with <38>surgical resection</38> first to assess extent of disease. Today patient also met with Drs. ***** and ***** regarding <39>L breast mastectomy</39> and <40>reconstruction</40> and has scheduled her <41>surgery</41> for 01/06/17. She had prior <42>biopsies</42> in both breasts several years ago which patient reports
