ner_results: ```plaintext
management recommendations were discussed at length with ***** and her two sisters who were present. ***** has undergone the surgical resection of her left breast <1>tumor</1> with <2>SLN assessment</2> as well. It is likely that she has additional <3>LNs</3> with metastatic disease. This is estimated to be about 64% by the <4>MSKCC normogram</4> and 44% by the ***** normogram. The role of <5>axillary dissection</5> and its pros/cons have been discussed with her by Dr. *****. ***** remains with a considerable risk of systemic relapse and mortality from this <6>cancer</6>. Although the most accurate risk assessment is not possible without quantitative <7>LN data</7> from an axillary dissection, her risk is clearly high. I estimate her risk to be on the order of 60% or higher. This can be reduced with the use of <8>adjuvant chemotherapy</8>, *****-targeting therapy, <9>hormonal therapy</9>, <10>radiotherapy</10>, and <11>bisphosphonate therapy</11>. These modalities were discussed. ***** will benefit from <12>adjuvant systemic chemotherapy</12>. Recommendation was made for <13>adjuvant AC/THP chemotherapy</13>. This consists of <14>AC x 4</14> given q2weeks with <15>growth factor support</15>, followed by 12 weeks of <16>taxol</16> along with one year of <17>trastuzumab</17> and <18>pertuzumab</18>. Side effects were discussed including potential for <19>nausea/vomiting</19>, <20>alopecia</20>, <21>bone marrow suppression</21> and <22>infections</22>, <23>cardiomyopathy</23>, <24>neuropathy</24>, and a small risk of <25>secondary leukemias</25>. As an alternative, we also discussed the <26>TCHP regimen</26>. This consists of 6 cycles of <27>TCHP</27> with one year of <28>trastuzumab/pertuzumab</28>. Side effects are similar with sparing of the cardiomyopathy and leukemogenic risks. We also discussed the use of <29>extended adjuvant neratinib</29> in year 2 including the potential for <30>diarrhea</30> and the need for prophylactic anti-*****. ***** will also benefit from <31>adjuvant hormone therapy</31>. A recommendation was made for <32>Arimidex 1 mg PO daily</32> for a duration of 10 years. This would begin at the completion of chemotherapy. Side effects were discussed.
``` 
