 note is my own.  I have reviewed the history and participated in the physical exam and assessment and plan as documented.    This is a shared visit for services provided by me, Dr. ***** *****, MD. I performed a face-to-face encounter with the patient and the following portion of the note is my own.      ***** ***** ***** is a 60 y.o. female with <1>Stage IIb (T2N1M0) Gr 2 IDC</1> <2>ER+/PR+/*****-</2>, +***** and <3>node positive left breast cancer</3> in April 2017. She had <4>chemotherapy</4>, <5>left partial mastectomy</5>, <6>XRT</6>. She started <7>letrozole</7> October 2017.    She reports tolerating <8>letrozole</8> well. Her <9>bone achiness</9> has improved. Occasionally feels <10>stiffness in her knee and fingers</10> when sitting still, resolves with movement.     She had <11>right chest wall pain</11> and <12>lump at the previous site of JP insertion</12> and was evaluated January 2019, which was normal.     She presents with a <13>skin cyst on her left palm</13> that she noticed about one week ago. Not painful.     Plans to travel to ***** ***** ***** ***** in August 2019.    On exam, <14>right lateral chest wall 1-2 mm density</14> consistent with a <15>stitch granuloma</15>  <16>Keloid scar on right upper chest at port site</16>  <17>Early *****'s contracture in left palm</17>, no impact on digits    IMP  ***** ***** ***** <18>ER+ breast cancer</18> s/p <19>TC x 6</19> on <20>letrozole</20> now x 1.5 years.  Tolerating therapy well.  Has some <21>pain in her right breast</21> on and off, overall evaluation negative.  Less <22>bone aching</22> now that she is exercising more!  Sometimes <23>stiff with sitting still</23>.    <24>Bone density April 2018</24> showed <25>osteoporosis in spine</25> and <26>osteopenia in femur</26>.  Taking <27>calcium</27> and <28>vitamin</28> and exercising.    Plan  <29>Bone density in early April</29>  Submit authorization for <30>zoledronate</30>  <31>Mammogram in May</31>.    Also discussed *****/6i as we are waiting on adjuvant data.    RTC 6 months    Patient ready and able to be educated, verbalizes understanding of information/instructions given.  Treatment options, side effects and nutrition reviewed in detail.  Total face to face time: 35  Total  counseling time: 30    *****, ***** ***** am acting as a scribe for services provided by ***** *****. *****, MD on *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM    The above scribed documentation accurately reflects the services I have provided.    ***** *****. *****, MD   *****/*****/***** 9:54 AM      
``` 
