<1>Laboratory</1>.    Methodology  Fixative:  <2>10% Neutral-buffered formalin</2>  <3>Cold ischemia time</3>: < 1 hour  <4>Duration of fixation</4>:  6-72 hours   <5>ER antibody clone</5>:  SP1 (*****)  <6>PR antibody clone</6>:  1E2 (*****)  ***** <7>antibody clone</7>: 4B5 (*****)            -Interpretive Criteria  -<8>ER/PR</8>:    Positive: reported when = 1% of tumor cells show nuclear staining.  Negative: reported when < 1% or 0% of tumor cells have nuclear staining.  <9>ER Low Positive</9> (Not PR): reported when 1-10% of tumor cell nuclei are  immunoreactive.      -*****:  Scoring Criterion and Scoring System:  <10>IHC Level of Expression</10> (Score) /<11>Tumor Cell Membrane Staining Pattern</11>  Positive 3+: Intense complete and circumferential membrane staining in  >10% of tumor cells  Equivocal 2+: Circumferential membrane staining that is either  non-uniform and/or weak/moderate in >10% of tumor cells, or intense  complete and circumferential membrane staining in = 10% of tumor cells.  Negative 1+: Incomplete membrane staining that is faint/barely  perceptible in >10% of tumor cells.  Negative 0: No staining observed or membrane staining that is incomplete  and faint/barely perceptible in = 10% of tumor cells.  Equivocal Category for ***** <12>IHC results</12>:  ***** ***** 2+ staining result that  is interpreted as equivocal may not show ***** amplification.    The following additional <13>immunohistochemical stains</13> were performed on  <14>block A14</14> to help establish the diagnosis:  - *****/6:  Patchy positive in <15>intraductal proliferation</15> at the margin,  supporting <16>usual ductal hyperplasia</16>  - <17>Synaptophysin</17>:  Negative   - <18>Chromogranin</18>:  Negative    The <19>specimen</19> was *****.  The <20>radiograph</20> was reviewed by the  pathologist and demonstrates the presence and location of a <21>biopsy clip</21>  and <22>mag seed</22>.  Tissue from these areas was specifically sampled for  <23>histologic evaluation</23> in order to help establish the diagnosis.    Dr. *****-***** ***** has also reviewed <24>slide A14</24> and agrees with  the  diagnosis.
``` 
