 position  03/26/19:<1>Mammogram</1> & <2>US</2>: <3>2.8 x 3.3 x 3.9 cm mass</3> in <4>left breast</4> at <5>3:30 position</5>, <6>3.2 cm from the nipple</6> with <7>multiple enlarged LNs</7> in <8>left axilla</8>; *****-5  04/01/19: <9>US guided core biopsy</9> of <10>left breast</10> and <11>L axillary LN</11>: <12>Intermediate grade IDC</12> (<13>ER+</13>/<14>PR+</14>/***** <15>2+ by IHC</15>, <16>negative by FISH</16>) [<17>w/DCIS</17>]. <18>L axillary LN positive</18>  04/03/19: <19>Breast MRI</19>: <20>3.8 cm lesion</20> in the <21>4:00 position</21>. <22>1 cm L axillary LN</22>. No other lesions or chest wall involvement  04/04/19: <23>PET/CT</23>: <24>Breast mass</24> measured <25>2.2 x 1.8 cm</25>. <26>2 enlarged hypermetabolic left axillary lymph nodes</26>, the largest measuring <27>10 mm in short axis dimension</27>. No distant metastasis  *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/*****: <28>4 cycles of dose dense AC</28> with Dr. ***** (*****)  <29>Germline genetic testing</29> with <30>Invitae panel of 47 genes</30> was <31>negative</31> (pt has copy of report)  05/24/19: <32>Breast US</32>: <33>Excellent response to treatment</33>  05/31/19: <34>Brain MRI</34>: <35>Negative for infarction or masses</35>  06/10/19: <36>Paclitaxel</36> started (held 1 week due to <37>neutropenia</37>)  06/24/19: <38>Paclitaxel</38> held again due to <39>elevated transaminases</39>  07/05/19: <40>Weekly Abraxane</40> started  08/30/19: <41>Completed Abraxane</41>  09/02/19: <42>Breast MRI</42>: <43>Dramatic response to therapy</43> and <44>near total complete resolution of the lesion and enhancement</44> in the <45>left breast</45> at <46>4:00 position</46>. <47>No significant residual or recurrent disease</47>
