ner_results: ```plaintext
<1>fasting</1> and a suitable delay of 60 minutes following the intravenous administration of <2>15.63 mCi 18F-FDG</2> at the right hand, <3>3D body imaging</3> is performed from the base of the skull to below the pelvis using the <4>General Electric Discovery ST PET/CT scanner</4>. Initially, a <5>low dose CT</5> is performed for <6>attenuation correction</6> and <7>anatomic correlation</7>. Subsequent <8>3.0 minute bed positions</8> were then performed for acquisition of the <9>PET data set</9> with subsequent fusion with the <10>CT</10> for the <11>diagnostic data set</11>. The patient's <12>blood glucose</12> at the time of injection was <13>88 mg/dL</13>. <14>RADIATION DOSIMETRY</14>: <15>CTDIvol</15>: <16>5.6 mGy</16> Total exam <17>DLP</17>: <18>497.85 mGy-cm</18> <19>COMPARISON</19>: <20>Pelvic ultrasound</20> from <21>10/23/2008</21>. <22>FINDINGS</22>: The distribution of <23>18F-FDG</23> in the visualized <24>brain</24>, <25>myocardium</25> and the <26>urinary tract</26> appears physiologic. Head and neck: There is no <27>hypermetabolic deep cervical lymphadenopathy</27>. Thorax: There is a <28>hypermetabolic mass</28> in the outer quadrant of the <29>left breast</29> with associated <30>clip</30>. The mass is <31>isodense</31> to the adjacent glandular tissue, measuring approximately <32>2.2 x 1.8 cm</32> with maximum <33>SUV 3.4</33>. Additional note is made of <34>2 enlarged hypermetabolic left axillary lymph node</34>. The larger and more hypermetabolic lymph node measures <35>10 mm</35> in short axis dimension with maximum <36>SUV 4.2</36>. No enlarged right metabolic <37>internal mammary lymph nodes</37> are identified. No <38>hypermetabolic hilar or mediastinal lymphadenopathy</38> is present. There are no <39>pulmonary nodules</39> or <40>pleural effusions</40>. The <41>heart size</41> appears normal. There is a <42>trace pericardial effusion</42>. Abdomen and pelvis: There are no <43>hypermetabolic lesions</43> in the <44>liver</44>, <45>adrenal glands</45> or <46>retroperitoneal lymph nodes</46>. There is a small <47>non-FDG avid low-density lesion</47> in <48>hepatic</48> *****, likely a <49>cyst</49>, measuring <50>7 mm</50>. The <51>uterus</51> is prominent in size. There is <52>focal linear uptake</52> within the right side of the uterus with maximum <53>SUV 4.5</53>.
``` 
