 and <1>FSH</1> once every 1-2 months until September 2020 at least. I stressed that it is important that she is confirmed to remain post-menopausal while on <2>letrozole</2>. We discussed that if she is not post-menopausal, we can administer <3>ovarian suppression shots</3> or she can have an <4>oophorectomy</4> performed. I also recommend a baseline <5>DEXA scan</5> to see if there is a need for a <6>bisphosphonate</6>. I explained that a <7>hysterectomy</7> is not necessary. Additionally, we discussed ***** and the results of the ***** study. I explained the recent press releases for both <8>palbociclib</8> (***** study) and publication of data on <9>abemaciclib</9> (*****) in the adjuvant setting. I explained that while <10>palbociclib</10> did not show an improvement in ***** at a median FUP of about 3 years in the ***** trial, ***** did show benefit in the ***** study. We also briefly discussed the ***** study. I reviewed the side effects of ***** including <11>diarrhea</11>. I explained that if the medication is too hard to tolerate at <12>300 mg</12> a day, she can discuss dose reduction with her oncologist. I also explained ***** guidelines regarding imaging and <13>tumour markers</13>. We discussed <14>Levulan PDT</14> and <15>vitamins/supplements</15> and I do not think there would be any interaction with <16>abemaciclib</16> I encouraged the patient to sign up for and utilize <17>Mychart</17> since this is the best way to communicate new information to me and to help determine whether a follow up visit is warranted I have reviewed and updated the patient's past medical history, medications, allergies, family and social histories. I spent a total of <18>60 minutes</18> face-to-face with the patient and <19>50 minutes</19> of that time was spent counseling regarding <20>Treatment options</20>, <21>side effects</21>, <22>clinical trials</22>, and <23>follow up plan</23>. Patient expresses understanding and agrees with the plan. *****, ***** ***** ***** am acting as a scribe for services provided by ***** ***** *****, MD on *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM The above scribed documentation accurately reflects the services I have provided. ***** ***** *****, MD *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM
