<1>triple negative breast cancer</1> and we would like to give her the best <2>chemotherapy regimen</2> possible to cure this disease. We recommend starting <3>Abraxane</3> now at a weekly dose for a total of 12 weeks which can replace the weekly <4>Taxol</4> in this regimen. <5>Abraxane</5> can be given at <6>100 mg/m2</6> weekly for a total of 12 weeks, which will give us three months' time to better manage her <7>diabetes</7> and hopefully at that time the <8>wound</8> will further heal. If at that time her general health condition improves, we would like to give her an additional two cycles of dose-dense <9>Adriamycin</9> plus <10>Cytoxan</10>. In general, we support this <11>chemotherapy</11> with ***** injection to prevent <12>neutropenia</12> or <13>neutropenic fever</13>. To further decrease her risk for an <14>infection</14>, we would also recommend starting her on <15>Levaquin</15> post dose-dense <16>AC cycle</16> to prevent <17>infection</17>. # We will also obtain her <18>pathology specimens</18> we reviewed here at <19>UCSF</19> and to repeat her <20>ER/PR</20> and <21>HER-2 status</21> and confirm that she has a negative status. # <22>Genetic counseling</22>. The patient developed <23>triple negative breast cancer</23> at the age of 53, and without family history we would like patient to meet with our <24>genetic counselor</24> to consider whether <25>genetic tests</25> would be needed to rule out <26>mutation</26>. We plan to start her <27>chemotherapy</27> on <28>06/05/2011</28> with prior <29>laboratory tests</29> to evaluate her <30>CBC</30>, <31>renal function</31>, and <32>liver function</32>. Thank you very much for referring this lovely patient to our care. ***** *****. *****, M.D. CLINICAL PROFESSOR OF MEDICINE <33>UCSF COMPREHENSIVE CANCER CENTER</33> ***** ***** ***** <34>BREAST CARE CENTER</34> I have seen and examined the patient. I have reviewed and discussed the case with Dr. ***** ***** and agree with the findings and treatment plan as documented above. EXTRA COPIES: CARBON COPIES: ***** ***** *****, MD 260
``` 
