Breast: Corresponding to site of proven <1>malignancy</1>, there is a <2>biopsy clip</2> in the upper central right breast, middle depth, with faint residual <3>non-mass enhancement</3> with slow persistent kinetics, spanning 14 x 16 x 8 mm (previously 27 x 14 x 9 mm). The <4>enhancement</4> is much less avid and confluent in comparison to the previous <5>MRI</5>. LEFT Breast: Corresponding to site of proven <6>malignancy</6>, there is faint residual <7>non-mass enhancement</7> with slow persistent kinetics spanning 30 x 13 x 23 mm in ***** x trans x CC extent (previously 34 x 16 x 24 mm) surrounding the <8>biopsy clip</8> in the upper outer quadrant of the left breast. The <9>enhancement</9> is much less avid and confluent in comparison to the previous <10>MRI</10>. Left axillary <11>node</11> have decreased in size and now have normal size/morphology. -03/20/20: <12>C4</12> ***** and <13>Cyclophosphamide</13> -03/29/20: <14>Pelvic US</14>: Normal appearance of the <15>uterus</15> and right <16>ovary</16> without associated mass. Left <17>ovary</17> is not seen; no left <18>adnexal mass</18>.  <19>Breast cancer</19> of lower-inner quadrant of right female breast (CMS code) 12/29/2019  <20>Malignant neoplasm</20> of upper-outer quadrant of left breast in female, <21>estrogen receptor positive</21> (CMS code) 11/23/2019  <22>BRCA1</22> ***** mutation positive 11/10/2019  <23>Anxiety</23> and <24>depression</24> 03/16/2019  History of *****'s <25>disease</25> 11/17/2014
