 in randomized trials (***** ***** *****)(***** ***** *****). Side effects of <1>tamoxifen</1> were discussed including potential for <2>hot flashes</2>, <3>mood effects</3>, increased incidence of <4>thromboembolic events</4> and <5>endometrial cancer</5> in postmenopausal women. Side effects of <6>AIs</6> were discussed including *****, <7>myalgias</7>, and potential acceleration of <8>bone loss</8>. Although <9>AIs</9> are restricted to the postmenopausal state, ***** has high risk disease and will benefit from the superior efficacy afforded by <10>AIs</10>. This was confirmed in the combined analysis of the <11>SOFT</11> and <12>TEXT trials</12> wherein <13>ovarian suppression</13> with <14>aromatase inhibitor therapy</14> was the optimal <15>hormonal therapy</15> modality in premenopausal patients (***** ***** *****). ***** will likely be peri-menopausal at the completion of <16>chemotherapy</16> and may require <17>ovarian suppression</17> for a period of time. Alternatively ***** therapy with continuous <18>estradiol monitoring</18> for a period of time may establish a permanent menopausal status without the need for suppression. The <19>bone loss</19> associated with postmenopausal use of <20>AIs</20> can be ***** with <21>anti-resorptive bone agents</21>. In addition to beneficial effects on bone, the use of ***** or <22>denosumab</22> every <23>6 months</23> for <24>3 years</24> in post-menopausal patients with early stage <25>breast cancer</25> is associated with a significant reduction in <26>breast cancer recurrence</26> (***** ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** *****), providing additional benefit to their use in this patient population. Side effects of <27>zoledronic acid</27> and <28>denosumab</28> were discussed including a rare risk of ***** with no cases confirmed in the *****-12 or *****-18 studies (***** ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** *****), but <29>2%</29> in the more intense schedule of the ***** trial (***** ***** *****), and a rare risk of <30>atypical femoral fractures</30> at a rate of under <31>0.2%</31> (***** ***** *****) with no cases confirmed in the *****-18 study (***** ***** *****). <32>Zoledronic infusions</32>
