eous material, which is unchanged compared to priors and was not hypermetabolic on prior <45>PET</45>. <46>Chest CT</46> showed no <47>intrathoracic metastatic disease</47>. 03/22/19 <48>a/c/p CT</48> - further mild decrease in size of multiple <49>hepatic metastatic lesions</49> as well as mild improvement in <50>periportal nodal conglomerate</50>. Unchanged <51>distention</51> of 
