ner_results: ```plaintext
activity (though evaluation of the brain on this study is limited). There is physiologic tonsillar, salivary gland, and oral activity. There is mild <1>atherosclerotic calcification</1> of the <2>carotid arteries</2>, left slightly greater than right. There is no discrete or intense <3>thyroid hypermetabolism</3>, nor intensely hypermetabolic <4>adenopathy</4> within the neck. Thorax: There is persistent subtle irregularity/nodularity of the bilateral <5>breast tissues</5>, similar to prior study. In particular, there is an approximately <6>1.4 cm faintly hypermetabolic density</6> within the <7>right lateral breast</7> on <8>CT images</8> 119-***** with <9>SUV 1.0</9> (previously similar in size with <10>SUV 0.8</10>). There are other very faintly hypermetabolic nodular densities within the both breasts, including an approximately <11>1 cm density</11> within the <12>right superolateral breast</12> (<13>CT image</13> 104, <14>SUV 1.2</14>) and an approximately <15>2 cm elongated density</15> within the <16>left lateral breast</16> (<17>CT images</17> 124-*****, <18>SUV 1.3</18>). These findings also appear relatively stable from prior study. There are no definitive new or intensely hypermetabolic <19>breast lesions</19> on either side. The numerous hypermetabolic <20>right axillary</20> and <21>right subpectoral lymph nodes</21> seen previously has significantly improved with interval therapy. For example, there is a residual <22>2.1 x 1.0 cm right axillary node</22> with an internal <23>biopsy clip/marker</23> on <24>CT image</24> 90 with <25>SUV 1.9</25> (previously <26>2.3 x 1.5 cm</26> with <27>SUV 15.1</27>), as well as a residual <28>1.2 x 1.0 cm right lateral subpectoral node</28> on <29>CT images</29> 83-84 with <30>SUV 1.8</30> (previously <31>1.8 x 1.6 cm</31> with <32>SUV 9.6</32>). There are other scattered residual <33>right axillary</33> and <34>right subpectoral nodes</34> that have similarly significantly declined in size from prior study, and now demonstrate little (if any) appreciable metabolic activity. These findings are consistent with extensive locoregional nodal <35>metastatic disease</35> that has substantially improved with
