ner_results: ```plaintext
ninth rib. These prior findings were equivocal, with limited, treated/resolved (by metabolism) skeletal metastatic disease not entirely excluded. However, there is currently felt to be no definitive metabolic evidence of active skeletal metastatic disease. For reference/comparison purposes, <1>blood pool activity</1> within the <2>descending thoracic aorta</2> (at the level of the carina) demonstrates an approximate <3>SUV</3> of <4>2.0</4> currently and <5>2.2</5> previously. Other Result Information Ifc, ***** Amb ***** Results In - *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM PST PROCEDURE: <6>PET SKULL BASE MID THIGH W ATTENUATION CT</6> ***** *****, *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM STUDY: <7>F-18 FDG Whole Body PET/CT Study</7> CLINICAL INDICATION: 77-year-old woman with a history of <8>right breast invasive lobular carcinoma</8> with <9>right axillary nodal metastatic involvement</9>, treated with <10>letrozole</10> (since <11>December 2019</11>). <12>Restaging evaluation/assessment of response to therapy</12>. COMPARISON: Prior <13>PET/CT</13> at ***** ***** ***** Imaging Center on <14>10/31/2019</14>. A <15>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis</15> on <16>12/06/2019</16> and a <17>whole body bone scan</17> on <18>11/21/2019</18> are also reviewed. TECHNIQUE: At the time of this study, the patient's <19>fasting blood glucose</19> was <20>93 mg/dL</20> and her <21>weight</21> was <22>199 lbs</22>. Approximately <23>70 minutes</23> after the intravenous administration of <24>12.0 mCi of 18-FDG</24>, <25>PET emission images</25> and <26>CT (dose-limited, without CT contrast) transmission images</26> were acquired from the top of the head to the mid thighs. The PET images were subsequently corrected for <27>tissue attenuation</27>, fused with the CT images, and reconstructed for review in orthogonal and <28>3D rotating (MIP) projections</28>. (<29>CT dose information</29>: <30>CTDIvol</30> = <31>9.9 mGy</31>, <32>DLP</32> = <33>956.50 mGy-cm</33>) FINDINGS: Head and Neck: There is relatively symmetric physiologic <34>brain activity</34> (though evaluation of the brain on this study is limited). There is physiologic <35>tonsillar</35>, <36>salivary gland</36>, and <37>oral activity</37>.
``` 
