nodes by <1>CT</1> criteria.    Heterogeneous <2>thyroid gland</2> with <3>hypoattenuating nodules</3>.    Small left <4>pleural effusion</4> with associated <5>compressive atelectasis</5> and/or <6>consolidation</6>. No suspicious <7>pulmonary nodules</7> or <8>masses</8> identified. No <9>pneumothorax</9>.    No <10>cardiomegaly</10> or <11>pericardial effusion</11>. There is a <12>3 vessel left-sided aortic arch</12>. The great vessels are widely patent. Normal caliber <13>thoracic aorta</13> without <14>dissection</14>. No <15>periaortic inflammatory stranding</15> or <16>free fluid</16>. No filling defects within the <17>central pulmonary arteries</17>.    Extensive <18>osseous metastatic disease</18> involving the <19>axial/appendicular</19> ***** with old <20>sternal</20> and <21>bilateral rib pathologic fracture deformities</21> with <22>callus formation</22>.    <23>ABDOMEN/PELVIS</23>  Numerous <24>hypoattenuating lesions</24> scattered throughout the right and left <25>hepatic lobes</25> (series 3, images 98, 105, 106, 110, 116, 117, 119, 124, 125, 127, 131, 140, and 148), worrisome for <26>metastatic disease</26>, increased in size and in number when compared to study dated <27>03/10/2020</27>. The index lesions are as follows:      1. <28>Hepatic</28> ***** <29>mass</29> measures <30>2.3 cm</30> (December 115), previously <31>1.2 cm</31>.  2. <32>Mass</32> <33>hepatic segment VIII</33> measures <34>2.1 cm</34> (December 129), previously <35>1 cm</35>.  3. <36>Mass</36> <37>hepatic segment VIII</37> measures <38>2.1 cm</38> (December 117), new when compared to recent prior imaging.    No <39>intra-/extrahepatic biliary duct dilatation</39>. <40>Decompressed gallbladder</40> without <41>radiopaque stones</41>. The <42>hepatic and portal veins</42> are patent. There is conventional <43>hepatic arterial anatomy</43>.    No <44>splenomegaly</44>. Subtle areas of <45>heterogeneity</45> within the mid <46>pancreas</46>, possibly related to <47>contrast bolus timing</47> with underlying <48>mass lesions</48> not excluded. Normal <49>pancreas</49> without <50>duct dilatation</50>, <51>atrophy</51>, or <52>focal mass lesions</52>.    The <53>adrenal glands</53> are symmetric bilaterally without <54>nodularity</54> or <55>hyperplasia</55>. The <56>kidneys</56> demonstrate symmetric enhancement without <57>hydronephrosis</57> or <58>radiopaque stones</58>. The <59>urinary bladder</59> is within normal limits.    <60>Lobular uterine contours</60>
