 with a calcified <1>fundal uterine myoma</1>. No suspicious <2>adnexal mass lesions</2> identified.    The loops of small and large bowel are normal in caliber without evidence of <3>obstruction</3> or <4>ileus</4>. Large amount of stool throughout the colon, possibly reflecting <5>constipation</5>. No <6>pneumoperitoneum</6> or <7>free fluid</7>. The appendix is within normal limits.    No pathologically enlarged <8>retroperitoneal</8>, <9>mesenteric</9>, or <10>pelvic sidewall lymph nodes</10> by <11>CT</11> criteria.    Normal <12>abdominal aortic diameter</12> (<13>3cm</13>).   The <14>celiac</14> *****, <15>SMA</15>, <16>bilateral renal arteries</16>, and ***** are patent. The <17>IVC</17> is patent.    Extensive <18>osseous metastatic disease</18> involving the <19>axial/appendicular</19> ***** with old <20>lower lumbar spine</20> and <21>left inferior pubic ramus pathologic fracture deformities</21>. Status post <22>left hip arthroplasty</22>. There is suggestion of additional <23>pathologic fracture deformities</23> involving the <24>left acetabulum</24>    ***** IMPRESSION *****:  1. <25>Pathologic right axillary mediastinal lymphadenopathy</25>, worrisome for <26>nodal metastatic disease</26>, stable in size when compared to study dated <27>03/10/2020</27>.    2. Multiple <28>hypoattenuating lesions</28> scattered throughout the <29>right and left hepatic lobes</29>, worrisome for <30>metastatic disease</30>, increased in size and in number when compared to study dated <31>03/10/2020</31>.    3. Extensive <32>blastic osseous metastatic disease</32> involving the visualized portions of the <33>axial/appendicular</33> ***** with <34>lower lumbar spine</34>, <35>left inferior pubic ramus</35>, probable <36>left acetabular</36>, <37>sternal</37>, and <38>multiple rib pathologic fracture deformities</38>, not significantly changed in appearance when compared to study dated <39>03/10/2020</39>. Please note the patient's extensive <40>osseous tumor burden</40> extensive difficult to assess for subtle changes in disease state.    4. <41>Small left pleural effusion</41> with associated <42>compressive atelectasis</42> and/or <43>consolidation</43>.         PATHOLOGY:    <44>11/07/19 Right axillary LN core needle biopsy</44>  Collected: <45>11/07/2019</45>          Case #: *****-2442       
