ner_results: ```plaintext
 were positive and <1>HER-2/neu</1> was negative.  The <2>tumor grade</2> was assessed as <3>2</3>.    A long discussion with Ms. ***** about the general approach to the treatment of primary <4>breast cancer</4> with the use of <5>surgery</5> and <6>radiation</6> to remove the <7>tumor</7> from the <8>chest wall</8> and prevent its recurrence locally as well as the use of <9>chemotherapy</9> and <10>hormonal therapy</10> as systemic therapy peak to prevent distant metastatic recurrence. Given the <11>tumor parameters</11> mentioned above I assessed that she had a reasonably high risk of <12>breast cancer recurrence</12> in the range of about <13>40-45%</13>. I discussed the process of risk estimation with her and the various parameters that we use to assess risk she seemed to understand as well.  Ms. ***** that it would be very reasonable to pursue a course of <14>hormonal therapy</14> to decrease the risk of <15>metastatic recurrence</15> and that the risk-benefit ratio for <16>hormonal treatment</16> would be favorable. Although I believe there would be some benefit from a course of <17>chemotherapy</17> in this case I believe her age (even though she appears vigorous for her stated age) and her history of <18>Parkinson's disease</18> would make the risk benefit ratio for a course of <19>chemotherapy</19> less favorable.  Since a course of <20>chemotherapy</20> added to a course of <21>hormonal therapy</21> only give her an additional benefit of <22>3-4%</22> I suggested I could not strongly recommend a course of <23>chemotherapy</23> that would be a personal decision will depend on how aggressively she wanted to approach his situation with Ms. ***** told me that she was leaning against the course of <24>chemotherapy</24> and would prefer to receive a course of <25>hormonal therapy</25> alone and I to initiate therapy could support her in that decision.  Plan:     Ms. ***** will return to ***** ***** medical oncologist Dr. ***** for further discussions and definitive treatment          
