 is well supported by her family and husband.     Assessment / Plan:    1. <1>Stage I left breast cancer</1> <2>s/p lumpectomy</2> and <3>sentinel node</3> March 2020 and <4>radiation</4>.  <5>9 mm tumor</5>, <6>G2</6>, <7>node negative</7>, <8>ER</8> and <9>PR</9> and <10>AR positive</10> and <11>her 2 negative</11>.   2.  <12>S/p radiation</12> to the <13>left breast</13>.   3.  I discussed the role of <14>hormone blockade</14> to decrease the risk of <15>systemic recurrence</15>.  She will proceed with <16>tamoxifen</16>. She is <17>perimenopausal</17>.  ***** plan to change to an ***** midway.   4.  RTC in 2-3 months for an exam to the ***** clinic.    5.  <18>Mammogram</18> in <19>February 2021</19>.   6.  ***** get her <20>genomic profile</20> of her <21>tumor</21>, she was told it was <22>low risk</22> so no <23>chemotherapy</23> given.         ***** ***** *****, MD  <24>Medical Oncology/Hematology</24>    TIME SPENT: 65  minutes examining patient, reviewing chart, coordinating care, discussing with patient and/or family.      I performed this evaluation using real-time <25>telehealth tools</25>, including a live video connection between my location and the patient's location. Prior to initiating, I obtained informed verbal consent to perform this evaluation using <26>telehealth tools</26> and answered all the questions about the telehealth interaction.               
